# Hanami palette service (`apps/palette`)

## Structure

```
slices/colour/
  actions/       one class per HTTP endpoint
  contracts/     dry-validation input schemas
  repos/         ROM or plain PG access for palette_data
lib/
  palette_extractor.rb   wraps vibrant_palette
  colour_matcher.rb      CIELAB distance, ranking
```

## Patterns

- Actions are small; validate with contracts before work
- Prefer `Dry::Monads` Result for operations that can fail (missing file, corrupt image)
- Inject dependencies — no global constants for DB or config
- JSON responses: `{ artworks: [...], meta: { count, query_ms } }`

## Colour math

- Extract with `vibrant_palette` (MMCQ swatches)
- Compare in **CIELAB**, not RGB
- Document known failure modes: same hue ≠ visual similarity

## Endpoints (Phase 1)

- `POST /colour/extract` — artwork id or image upload → palette jsonb
- `GET /colour/similar/:artwork_id` — nearest neighbours
- `POST /colour/match-room` — photo upload → ranked artworks
